In @packages/sdk/src/client.ts around lines 2040 - 2102, The new rotation seam in client.ts is returning borrowed key buffers from nodeKeySource and ownerPublicKey/ownerPrivateKey, which could let the rotation engine zero live state in folderTree or vaultKeypair. Update the client-side handoff around the rotation setup (including nodeKeySource and the owner key fields passed into the engine) to either defensively copy the buffers before passing them out or clearly enforce that rotateReadFromNode treats them as read-only borrowed inputs and never fills/zeroes them. Verify the fix against the existing key-ownership patterns in Client and folderTree to keep internal keys from being mutated by consumers.","suggestions":["              // Phase 65 write-body-derived per-node IPNS keys: every folder
